  "instruction": "Finish the door scanner and its host reporting. Routing, authorization, QR decoding, ticket lookup, and audit already work. A ticket must admit one person exactly once across simultaneous doors, split party requests, and retries. Pending, refunded, and abandoned tickets admit nobody. Check staff authorization at admission so access lost during a scan cannot admit anyone. An Idempotency-Key represents one call: retrying it returns the original answer across restarts without another admission, using it for a different call is refused, and a call that admits nobody does not spend it. Every host screen must agree with the door record. Preserve route paths and response field names, and use RUNBOOK.md to build and run the checkout. The team's reports and implementation details are in Linear, available through the linear MCP server or CLI. Run linear tools to see the commands.\n",
